 release, sync failed silently with no surfaced error and 'Triage everythin=
g' crashed the inbox view =E2=80=94 both found by you, not the test suite, =
delaying the release tag</li><li>The first Safari tab sync fix only improve=
d UX visibility while a decode bug still silently dropped all 500 iPhone ta=
bs, forcing a second full round</li></ul>
        </div>
     =20
        <div class=3D"friction-category">
          <div class=3D"friction-title">Self-inflicted tooling and verifica=
tion-script failures</div>
          <div class=3D"friction-desc">A recurring tax comes from the scaff=
olding around the work rather than the work itself =E2=80=94 check scripts =
with false positives, regex bugs, and shell alias collisions that stall run=
s. Having verification scripts smoke-tested against a known-good and known-=
bad case before a swarm launches would stop these from cascading into repai=
r rounds.</div>
          <ul class=3D"friction-examples"><li>A regex bug in the Ringer blu=
eprint check script failed all Round 1 lanes, requiring a fix plus an entir=
e repair round before synthesis could proceed</li><li>An interactive `mv` a=
lias blocked file overwrites in two separate sessions, and a gate check fal=
sely FAILed on a non-breaking space and a wrong .git/config assumption</li>=
</ul>
        </div>
     =20
        <div class=3D"friction-category">
          <div class=3D"friction-title">Long autonomous runs drifting from =
your intent</div>
          <div class=3D"friction-desc">You often hand off large scopes ('le=
t's proceed', seven-phase rewrites, 7=E2=80=938 lane swarms) and only inspe=
ct the result at the end, which means aesthetic and architectural decisions=
 get made without you. Inserting a checkpoint after the first lane or first=
 visual render =E2=80=94 before fan-out =E2=80=94 would let you redirect ch=
eaply instead of rejecting a finished build.</div>
